---
// Schematic drawings of charging connections. Not to scale.
---
<figure class="fig">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="cp-t cp-d" width="760" height="250">
    <title id="cp-t">Four ways a Kindle charges</title>
    <desc id="cp-d">Schematic drawings of a micro-USB plug with a tapered shape, a USB-C plug with a rounded symmetric shape, a Qi wireless charging pad under a Kindle, and a pogo-pin charging dock with metal contacts.</desc>
    <g font-family="sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="#1d1b18" text-anchor="middle">
      <!-- micro-USB -->
      <g transform="translate(20,10)">
        <rect x="20" y="62" width="100" height="42" rx="6" fill="#6b665c"/>
        <path d="M120 66 H150 L158 74 V92 L150 100 H120 Z" fill="#b9ad94" stroke="#1d1b18" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="128" y="76" width="22" height="14" rx="2" fill="#4a453d"/>
        <text x="90" y="150" font-weight="700">Micro-USB</text>
        <text x="90" y="168" fill="#4a453d">Tapered, one way up</text>
        <text x="90" y="186" fill="#4a453d">Older Kindles</text>
      </g>
      <!-- USB-C -->
      <g transform="translate(210,10)">
        <rect x="20" y="62" width="100" height="42" rx="6" fill="#6b665c"/>
        <rect x="120" y="66" width="38" height="34" rx="16" fill="#b9ad94" stroke="#1d1b18" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="127" y="76" width="24" height="14" rx="7" fill="#4a453d"/>
        <text x="90" y="150" font-weight="700">USB-C</text>
        <text x="90" y="168" fill="#4a453d">Rounded, either way up</text>
        <text x="90" y="186" fill="#4a453d">Newer Kindles</text>
      </g>
      <!-- Qi -->
      <g transform="translate(400,10)">
        <rect x="20" y="130" width="140" height="14" rx="6" fill="#4a453d"/>
        <rect x="45" y="20" width="90" height="106" rx="6" fill="#2f5d57"/>
        <rect x="53" y="30" width="74" height="78" rx="2" fill="#faf6ee" stroke="#1d1b18"/>
        <path d="M70 134 q20 -10 40 0 M62 140 q28 -16 56 0" fill="none" stroke="#faf6ee" stroke-width="2"/>
        <text x="90" y="174" font-weight="700">Qi wireless pad</text>
        <text x="90" y="192" fill="#4a453d">Signature Editions from 2021 and 2024</text>
        <text x="90" y="210" fill="#4a453d">Needs a pad that fits</text>
      </g>
      <!-- pogo -->
      <g transform="translate(590,10)">
        <rect x="30" y="140" width="110" height="16" rx="6" fill="#4a453d"/>
        <rect x="52" y="62" width="70" height="80" rx="4" fill="#6b665c"/>
        <circle cx="75" cy="124" r="4" fill="#d9b84a"/><circle cx="87" cy="124" r="4" fill="#d9b84a"/><circle cx="99" cy="124" r="4" fill="#d9b84a"/>
        <rect x="58" y="12" width="58" height="100" rx="5" fill="#2f5d57" transform="rotate(-6 87 62)"/>
        <rect x="64" y="22" width="46" height="72" rx="2" fill="#faf6ee" stroke="#1d1b18" transform="rotate(-6 87 62)"/>
        <text x="85" y="182" font-weight="700">Pogo-pin dock</text>
        <text x="85" y="200" fill="#4a453d">Contacts on the back</text>
        <text x="85" y="218" fill="#4a453d">2026 Signature Editions</text>
      </g>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>Our own schematic, not to scale and not based on any specific product. Which Kindle uses which connection is in the table below.</figcaption>
</figure>
